R2 is built. What I changed (all inside `code_map/src/`):

**`links.ts`** — calls dispatched through a service type now resolve by type, not by name:
- `memberDeclaration()` — when the checker points at a written shape (`readonly assert: (…) => T`), the member it belongs to is the declaration, so the link carries the interface member as `declaration` and is `kind: "service-call"`.
- `implementationsOfMember()` — implementations of a member are the class members that carry it **plus** the written objects that stand for it: every object literal whose contextual/annotated type is that service type. A shorthand `Service.of({ get })` resolves through `getShorthandAssignmentValueSymbol` to the variable it names (an implementation, not a call).
- `findCallers()` — a site reaches a function when its callee resolves to the function itself **or** to a member the function implements.
- Per-run caches on `Project` (`implementationsByMember`, `writtenObjects`) replaced a per-source-file cache that also keyed every member of one type to the first member looked up.

**`project.ts`** — the `cache` on `Project` plus the `WrittenObject` shape. **`nodes.ts`** — `propertyNameText` exported.

Generality (no fixture names, ids or lines anywhere in `src/`): verified with a held-out copy from `eval/holdout.ts --seed 42` (renamed identifiers, shifted lines) — 51 MET, 0 NOT MET; and a scratch project using `type Shape = { run(): number }` plus an inline annotated shape, which the owner-symbol lookup now resolves.

